ITEMS = ((('how do i check breathing in an emergency', 'what is the right way to check breathing', 'how to check breathing on an adult', 'how should i check breathing of a casualty', 'what to look for when checking breathing', 'how long should i spend checking breathing', 'how do you check breathing properly', 'steps for checking breathing in first aid', 'how can i tell if breathing is normal', 'what does checking breathing involve'), 'To check breathing, watch the chest for movement and listen or feel for air at the mouth for a few moments. Normal breathing is quiet and regular, while gasping is not normal. Call emergency services if breathing is absent or difficult, and start CPR if it has stopped.'), (('what is normal breathing when checking someone', 'how can checking breathing show a problem', 'what does abnormal breathing look like', 'how to spot shallow breathing in a casualty', 'what if breathing sounds noisy while checking', 'how to tell gasping from normal breathing', 'what breathing sign needs urgent help', 'how to judge if breathing is adequate', 'what changes in breathing should i watch for', 'how do i describe breathing to an operator when checking breathing'), 'Normal breathing is steady and quiet. Noisy, shallow, very fast or gasping breaths suggest the person needs urgent assessment. Call emergency services and describe exactly what you saw while checking breathing, even if the person is still responsive.'), (('how long should i check breathing before cpr', 'what if i need longer to check breathing', 'should i check breathing twice', 'how many seconds for checking breathing', 'what if breathing is hard to see', 'should i check breathing before calling for help', 'how quickly to assess breathing', 'what if the person is very still when checking breathing', 'how long to watch the chest rise when checking breathing', 'when to stop checking and start treatment'), 'Spend only a brief moment checking breathing, as treatment should not be delayed. If there is no normal breath, call emergency services and start CPR. If you are unsure, ask the operator to guide you while you watch the chest.'), (('how do i check breathing in a baby', "what to watch when checking a child's breathing", 'is checking breathing different for infants', "how to see a baby's chest move when checking breathing", 'what if a child breathes fast', 'how to check breathing in a toddler', 'what signs of breathing trouble in children when checking breathing', 'should i wake a child to check breathing', 'when to call help after checking child breathing', "who should check a sick child's breathing"), 'For a baby or child, watch the chest and belly and listen near the mouth rather than disturbing them. Fast, noisy or laboured breaths need prompt advice. Call emergency services if breathing is very difficult, pauses, or the child becomes drowsy.'), (('what if the person is gasping when i check breathing', 'is gasping normal breathing when checking breathing', 'should i start cpr for gasping when checking breathing', 'how to respond to agonal breathing', 'what if breathing comes in slow gasps', 'why is gasping not normal when checking breathing', 'what to tell the operator about gasping when checking breathing', 'how to check for a pulse after gasping', 'what if gasping stops while waiting when checking breathing', 'when to call emergency services for gasping when checking breathing'), 'Gasping is not normal breathing and should be treated as a cardiac arrest. Call emergency services and begin CPR with chest compressions. Tell the operator about the gasping so they can advise, and continue until a qualified person arrives.'), (('how do i check breathing after an injury', 'should i move someone to check breathing', 'what if a fall makes breathing difficult', 'how to check breathing with a chest injury', 'what if the person is trapped when checking breathing', 'how to check breathing after a head injury when checking breathing', 'what if checking breathing causes pain', 'how to watch breathing while keeping still', 'when to call help after an injury when checking breathing', 'who can assess breathing at an incident'), 'Check breathing without moving the person unnecessarily, especially after a fall or suspected spinal injury. Look for chest movement and listen for air. Call emergency services if breathing is difficult or the person is unwell.'), (('what to do if checking breathing shows it has stopped', 'should i start rescue breaths', 'how to act when there is no breathing', 'what if the chest is not moving when checking breathing', 'how to open the airway before breathing help', 'should i call first when breathing stops', 'what if i am alone and breathing has stopped', 'how to begin cpr after checking breathing', 'what if breathing returns', 'who takes over when breathing stops'), 'If checking breathing shows it has stopped, call emergency services and start CPR with chest compressions. If you are trained, give rescue breaths as well. Keep going until breathing returns or a qualified person takes over.'), (('how do i check the airway before checking breathing', 'should i tilt the head to check breathing', 'what if the tongue blocks the airway when checking breathing', 'how to lift the chin safely when checking breathing', 'should i look inside the mouth first when checking breathing', 'what if the person has vomit near the mouth when checking breathing', 'how to clear the airway gently when checking breathing', 'what if a neck injury is suspected when checking breathing', 'when to call for airway help when checking breathing', 'who can advise about airway positioning when checking breathing'), 'Open the airway by tilting the head back and lifting the chin, unless a neck injury is suspected. Look in the mouth and remove only an obvious object. Call emergency services if breathing is noisy or difficult, and follow their guidance.'), (('how can i check breathing without touching someone', 'what if i do not want to put my face near when checking breathing', 'is a mirror useful for checking breathing', 'can i see breath on a cold day', 'what if i cannot hear breathing clearly', 'how to check from a safe distance', 'what if the person is wearing a mask when checking breathing', 'how to observe chest movement when checking breathing', 'when to ask a bystander to check', 'who should get close to check breathing'), 'You can watch the chest and shoulders for movement without touching, and look for misting on a cool surface if available. If you cannot judge breathing, treat it as absent. Call emergency services and start CPR rather than waiting.'), (('when should i call emergency services after checking breathing', 'what breathing signs require urgent help', 'should i call if breathing is noisy', 'what if breathing seems fine but the person is drowsy', 'how urgent is shallow breathing', 'what to report after checking breathing', 'should i stay with someone with odd breathing', 'when to seek advice from a pharmacist when checking breathing', 'what if breathing changes during the night', 'who can review breathing problems'), 'Call emergency services if breathing is absent, gasping, very noisy or difficult, or if the person is drowsy. Tell the operator what you observed. A doctor should also review repeated breathing problems, even when the person seems to recover.'))
